const SN_BANK = [{"id":1,"concept":"ASA Classification","stem":"A client has controlled hypertension with no functional limitation. Which ASA classification is most appropriate?","choices":["ASA I","ASA II","ASA III","ASA IV"],"answer":1,"why":"ASA II describes a client with a mild, well-controlled systemic condition that does not limit normal activity.","zh":"ASA II 适用于患有轻度、控制良好的全身性疾病且日常活动不受限的患者。","rationales":[{"en":"ASA I is reserved for a healthy client without systemic disease.","zh":"ASA I 仅适用于没有全身性疾病的健康患者。"},{"en":"Controlled hypertension fits mild systemic disease.","zh":"控制良好的高血压属于轻度全身性疾病。"},{"en":"ASA III is used when disease is severe or substantially limits activity.","zh":"ASA III 用于严重疾病或明显限制活动的情况。"},{"en":"ASA IV indicates severe disease that is a constant threat to life.","zh":"ASA IV 表示严重疾病持续威胁生命。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"ASA II describes a client with a mild, well-controlled systemic condition that does not limit normal activity."},{"id":2,"concept":"ASA Classification","stem":"A client with unstable angina has chest pain at rest. Which ASA classification best fits this client?","choices":["ASA II","ASA III","ASA IV","ASA VI"],"answer":2,"why":"Unstable angina represents severe systemic disease that is a constant threat to life, so ASA IV is appropriate.","zh":"不稳定型心绞痛属于持续威胁生命的严重全身性疾病，因此归为 ASA IV。","rationales":[{"en":"ASA II is too low because the condition is not mild or stable.","zh":"ASA II 过低，因为该病并非轻度或稳定。"},{"en":"ASA III may fit stable severe disease, but not an active constant threat to life.","zh":"ASA III 可用于稳定的严重疾病，但不适用于持续威胁生命的活动性疾病。"},{"en":"Rest pain from unstable angina is a constant life threat.","zh":"不稳定型心绞痛静息时疼痛持续威胁生命。"},{"en":"ASA VI is reserved for a declared brain-dead organ donor.","zh":"ASA VI 仅用于已判定脑死亡的器官捐献者。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Unstable angina represents severe systemic disease that is a constant threat to life, so ASA IV is appropriate."},{"id":3,"concept":"Hypertension","stem":"A client’s blood pressure is 182/112 mmHg before elective debridement. What is the best action?","choices":["Proceed normally","Proceed after 5 minutes if the client feels well","Defer elective care and arrange prompt medical evaluation","Give aspirin and continue"],"answer":2,"why":"A reading at or above 180/110 mmHg is a danger-zone result. Elective care should be deferred and medical evaluation arranged.","zh":"血压达到或超过 180/110 mmHg 属于危险范围，应推迟选择性治疗并安排尽快医学评估。","rationales":[{"en":"This pressure creates unacceptable stroke and cardiac risk for routine elective care.","zh":"该血压使常规选择性治疗中的卒中和心脏风险不可接受。"},{"en":"A short rest does not make a severe reading safe if it remains this high.","zh":"短暂休息不能使持续如此高的血压变得安全。"},{"en":"Deferral and medical evaluation address the immediate risk appropriately.","zh":"推迟治疗并进行医学评估可恰当处理即时风险。"},{"en":"Aspirin is not treatment for severe hypertension and may increase bleeding.","zh":"阿司匹林不能治疗重度高血压，还可能增加出血。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"A reading at or above 180/110 mmHg is a danger-zone result. Elective care should be deferred and medical evaluation arranged."},{"id":4,"concept":"Hypertension","stem":"Which appointment modification is most appropriate for a client with controlled hypertension?","choices":["Long afternoon appointment after fasting","Short morning appointment with stress reduction","Supine position for the entire visit regardless of symptoms","Avoid all local anesthetic"],"answer":1,"why":"Short morning visits and a calm environment help reduce endogenous catecholamine release and blood-pressure elevation.","zh":"短时上午预约及减压环境有助于减少内源性儿茶酚胺释放和血压升高。","rationales":[{"en":"Fasting and a long visit can increase stress and the risk of hypoglycemia.","zh":"空腹和长时间治疗会增加压力及低血糖风险。"},{"en":"Short morning care with stress reduction is preferred.","zh":"短时上午治疗并减压是首选。"},{"en":"Position should be individualized; rigidly keeping every client supine is inappropriate.","zh":"体位应个体化，所有患者都始终仰卧并不合适。"},{"en":"Controlled hypertension does not require avoiding all local anesthetic.","zh":"控制良好的高血压不需要完全避免局部麻醉剂。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Short morning visits and a calm environment help reduce endogenous catecholamine release and blood-pressure elevation."},{"id":5,"concept":"Angina and MI","stem":"A client with stable angina develops chest pain during treatment. What should be done first?","choices":["Continue treatment while monitoring","Stop treatment, position comfortably, and assist with prescribed nitroglycerin","Give insulin","Place the client in Trendelenburg position"],"answer":1,"why":"Treatment is stopped immediately, the client is positioned comfortably, and prescribed nitroglycerin is used while vital signs are monitored.","zh":"应立即停止治疗，使患者处于舒适体位，并协助使用处方硝酸甘油，同时监测生命体征。","rationales":[{"en":"Continuing treatment increases myocardial oxygen demand.","zh":"继续治疗会增加心肌耗氧量。"},{"en":"This sequence reduces demand and treats ischemic chest pain.","zh":"此顺序可降低耗氧并治疗缺血性胸痛。"},{"en":"Insulin has no role in angina management.","zh":"胰岛素不用于心绞痛处理。"},{"en":"Trendelenburg may worsen breathing and is not the routine position for angina.","zh":"特伦德伦堡体位可能加重呼吸，不是心绞痛的常规体位。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Treatment is stopped immediately, the client is positioned comfortably, and prescribed nitroglycerin is used while vital signs are monitored."},{"id":6,"concept":"Angina and MI","stem":"Chest pain is not relieved after three nitroglycerin doses given 5 minutes apart. What is the priority?","choices":["Resume care because the maximum dose was reached","Activate EMS and manage as possible myocardial infarction","Give an oral antihistamine","Ask the client to walk around"],"answer":1,"why":"Persistent pain after three nitroglycerin doses may indicate myocardial infarction and requires emergency activation.","zh":"三次硝酸甘油后胸痛仍未缓解可能提示心肌梗死，需启动急救系统。","rationales":[{"en":"Reaching the dose limit is a reason to escalate, not resume care.","zh":"达到剂量上限意味着需要升级处理，而不是恢复治疗。"},{"en":"Persistent ischemic pain requires EMS activation.","zh":"持续缺血性胸痛需要启动急救服务。"},{"en":"Antihistamines do not treat myocardial ischemia.","zh":"抗组胺药不能治疗心肌缺血。"},{"en":"Walking increases cardiac workload and may worsen ischemia.","zh":"走动会增加心脏负荷并可能加重缺血。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Persistent pain after three nitroglycerin doses may indicate myocardial infarction and requires emergency activation."},{"id":7,"concept":"Heart Failure","stem":"Which chair position is best for a client with congestive heart failure who becomes short of breath when lying flat?","choices":["Fully supine","Semi-supine or upright","Trendelenburg","Prone"],"answer":1,"why":"An upright or semi-supine position improves ventilation and reduces orthopnea in congestive heart failure.","zh":"直立或半仰卧体位可改善通气并减轻充血性心力衰竭患者的端坐呼吸。","rationales":[{"en":"Supine positioning can worsen pulmonary congestion and orthopnea.","zh":"仰卧位可加重肺淤血和端坐呼吸。"},{"en":"Semi-supine or upright positioning supports breathing.","zh":"半仰卧或直立位有助于呼吸。"},{"en":"Trendelenburg increases venous return and may worsen pulmonary congestion.","zh":"特伦德伦堡体位增加静脉回流，可能加重肺淤血。"},{"en":"Prone positioning is impractical and does not address orthopnea.","zh":"俯卧位不实用，也不能解决端坐呼吸。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"An upright or semi-supine position improves ventilation and reduces orthopnea in congestive heart failure."},{"id":8,"concept":"Cardiac Devices","stem":"A client has a pacemaker. Which device-related precaution is most relevant?","choices":["Use electrosurgery directly over the device","Avoid equipment that may cause electromagnetic interference unless compatibility is confirmed","Do not take blood pressure","Avoid all ultrasonic instrumentation permanently"],"answer":1,"why":"Electromagnetic interference may disrupt some cardiac devices, so compatibility and manufacturer guidance should be confirmed.","zh":"电磁干扰可能影响某些心脏装置，因此应确认设备兼容性并遵循制造商指导。","rationales":[{"en":"Direct electrosurgery near the device may create hazardous interference.","zh":"在装置附近直接使用电外科设备可能产生危险干扰。"},{"en":"Confirming compatibility is the appropriate precaution.","zh":"确认兼容性是恰当的预防措施。"},{"en":"Routine blood-pressure measurement is not prohibited by a pacemaker.","zh":"装有起搏器并不禁止常规测量血压。"},{"en":"A blanket permanent ban on all ultrasonics is unnecessarily broad.","zh":"永久全面禁止所有超声设备过于宽泛。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Electromagnetic interference may disrupt some cardiac devices, so compatibility and manufacturer guidance should be confirmed."},{"id":9,"concept":"Anticoagulants","stem":"A client taking warfarin needs nonsurgical periodontal debridement. What is the best approach?","choices":["Tell the client to stop warfarin independently","Review bleeding history and relevant INR information; use local hemostatic measures as needed","Cancel all dental hygiene care permanently","Give vitamin K before treatment"],"answer":1,"why":"Anticoagulants should not be stopped without prescriber direction. Bleeding risk is assessed and managed with local measures and medical consultation when indicated.","zh":"未经处方医生指示不得停用抗凝药。应评估出血风险，并在需要时采用局部止血措施和医学会诊。","rationales":[{"en":"Stopping warfarin without medical direction creates thromboembolic risk.","zh":"未经医学指导停用华法林会增加血栓栓塞风险。"},{"en":"Assessment plus local hemostasis is the appropriate strategy.","zh":"评估并结合局部止血是恰当策略。"},{"en":"Anticoagulation alone does not permanently prohibit dental hygiene care.","zh":"抗凝治疗本身并不永久禁止牙科卫生治疗。"},{"en":"Vitamin K is not routinely given by the dental hygienist before care.","zh":"牙科卫生师不应在治疗前常规给予维生素 K。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Anticoagulants should not be stopped without prescriber direction. Bleeding risk is assessed and managed with local measures and medical consultation when indicated."},{"id":10,"concept":"Stroke","stem":"Which finding is most suggestive of an acute stroke?","choices":["Bilateral gradual leg fatigue","Sudden unilateral facial droop and arm weakness","Chronic dry mouth","Slowly developing gingival enlargement"],"answer":1,"why":"Sudden one-sided facial weakness and arm weakness are classic FAST warning signs of stroke.","zh":"突然出现单侧面部下垂和手臂无力是 FAST 卒中警示征象。","rationales":[{"en":"Gradual bilateral fatigue is nonspecific and not a classic FAST pattern.","zh":"渐进性双侧疲劳并非典型 FAST 表现。"},{"en":"Sudden unilateral deficits strongly suggest stroke.","zh":"突然单侧神经功能缺损强烈提示卒中。"},{"en":"Dry mouth is not an acute focal neurologic deficit.","zh":"口干不是急性局灶性神经缺损。"},{"en":"Gingival enlargement is not a stroke sign.","zh":"牙龈增生不是卒中征象。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Sudden one-sided facial weakness and arm weakness are classic FAST warning signs of stroke."},{"id":11,"concept":"Stroke","stem":"A client suddenly develops facial droop, slurred speech, and arm weakness. What is the priority?","choices":["Finish polishing quickly","Record the findings and schedule a medical appointment next week","Call 911 immediately and note the time symptoms began","Give oral glucose"],"answer":2,"why":"Stroke is time-critical. EMS must be activated immediately and symptom-onset time documented.","zh":"卒中治疗争分夺秒，应立即拨打 911 并记录症状开始时间。","rationales":[{"en":"Continuing treatment wastes critical reperfusion time.","zh":"继续治疗会浪费宝贵的再灌注时间。"},{"en":"Delayed outpatient follow-up is unsafe for acute stroke signs.","zh":"对急性卒中征象安排延迟门诊随访并不安全。"},{"en":"Immediate EMS activation and onset timing are essential.","zh":"立即启动急救并记录发作时间至关重要。"},{"en":"Oral glucose is appropriate for conscious hypoglycemia, not presumed stroke.","zh":"口服葡萄糖适用于清醒的低血糖患者，而非疑似卒中。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Stroke is time-critical. EMS must be activated immediately and symptom-onset time documented."},{"id":12,"concept":"Seizure","stem":"During a generalized tonic-clonic seizure, what should the clinician do?","choices":["Restrain the client’s limbs","Place an object between the teeth","Clear nearby objects, protect the head, and time the seizure","Give water immediately"],"answer":2,"why":"The priority is injury prevention: clear the area, protect the head, maintain safety, and time the event.","zh":"首要任务是防止受伤：清理周围物品、保护头部、维持安全并记录发作时间。","rationales":[{"en":"Restraint can cause musculoskeletal injury.","zh":"强行约束可造成肌肉骨骼损伤。"},{"en":"Nothing should be placed in the mouth during a seizure.","zh":"癫痫发作时不应将任何物品放入口中。"},{"en":"Protecting the client and timing the seizure are appropriate.","zh":"保护患者并记录发作时间是恰当措施。"},{"en":"Water creates aspiration risk during impaired consciousness.","zh":"意识受损时给水会增加误吸风险。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"The priority is injury prevention: clear the area, protect the head, maintain safety, and time the event."},{"id":13,"concept":"Seizure","stem":"When should EMS generally be activated for a seizure?","choices":["Every absence seizure lasting 5 seconds","When the seizure lasts more than 5 minutes or repeats without recovery","Only if the client bites the tongue","Never if the client has epilepsy"],"answer":1,"why":"A seizure lasting more than 5 minutes or recurrent seizures without recovery may represent status epilepticus and requires EMS.","zh":"癫痫持续超过 5 分钟或反复发作且未恢复可能为癫痫持续状态，需要急救服务。","rationales":[{"en":"A brief typical absence seizure does not automatically require EMS.","zh":"短暂的典型失神发作不一定需要急救。"},{"en":"Prolonged or repetitive seizures are medical emergencies.","zh":"长时间或反复癫痫发作属于医疗急症。"},{"en":"Tongue biting alone is not the main activation criterion.","zh":"单纯咬舌并非主要启动急救标准。"},{"en":"A known epilepsy diagnosis does not make prolonged seizures safe.","zh":"已知癫痫诊断并不意味着长时间发作是安全的。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"A seizure lasting more than 5 minutes or recurrent seizures without recovery may represent status epilepticus and requires EMS."},{"id":14,"concept":"Parkinson Disease","stem":"Which dental-care modification is most helpful for a client with Parkinson disease?","choices":["Schedule during the client’s best medication-controlled period and use short appointments","Withhold all Parkinson medication","Use long late-day appointments","Place the client fully supine despite swallowing difficulty"],"answer":0,"why":"Short visits timed to peak medication effectiveness improve motor control and cooperation.","zh":"将短时预约安排在药物效果最佳时段，可改善运动控制和配合度。","rationales":[{"en":"Timing care to the best “on” period is helpful.","zh":"将治疗安排在最佳“开期”有帮助。"},{"en":"Withholding medication may worsen rigidity and tremor.","zh":"停药可能加重僵硬和震颤。"},{"en":"Late-day fatigue can worsen motor symptoms.","zh":"晚间疲劳可能加重运动症状。"},{"en":"A more upright position may be safer when dysphagia or aspiration risk is present.","zh":"存在吞咽困难或误吸风险时，更直立的体位更安全。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Short visits timed to peak medication effectiveness improve motor control and cooperation."},{"id":15,"concept":"Dementia","stem":"Which communication strategy is best for a client with dementia?","choices":["Give several complex instructions at once","Use short, simple instructions and one step at a time","Speak only to the caregiver and ignore the client","Change the routine at every visit"],"answer":1,"why":"Simple one-step instructions reduce cognitive load and support participation.","zh":"简短、一次一步的指令可减轻认知负担并促进配合。","rationales":[{"en":"Multiple complex instructions can increase confusion.","zh":"多个复杂指令会增加困惑。"},{"en":"One-step communication is easier to process.","zh":"一次一步更容易理解。"},{"en":"The client should remain involved to the greatest extent possible.","zh":"应尽可能让患者参与。"},{"en":"Consistency and familiar routines are generally helpful.","zh":"保持一致和熟悉的流程通常更有帮助。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Simple one-step instructions reduce cognitive load and support participation."},{"id":16,"concept":"Diabetes","stem":"A conscious client with diabetes becomes shaky, sweaty, and confused. What is the most likely problem?","choices":["Hyperglycemia","Hypoglycemia","Hypertensive crisis","Anaphylaxis"],"answer":1,"why":"Rapid onset of sweating, tremor, hunger, and confusion is characteristic of hypoglycemia.","zh":"突然出现出汗、震颤、饥饿和意识混乱是低血糖的典型表现。","rationales":[{"en":"Hyperglycemia usually develops more gradually with thirst and frequent urination.","zh":"高血糖通常更缓慢出现，并伴口渴和尿频。"},{"en":"These adrenergic and neuroglycopenic signs fit hypoglycemia.","zh":"这些肾上腺素能和神经缺糖征象符合低血糖。"},{"en":"Hypertensive crisis does not typically cause this classic cluster.","zh":"高血压危象通常不会出现这一典型组合。"},{"en":"Anaphylaxis usually includes airway, breathing, skin, or circulatory signs.","zh":"过敏性休克通常包括气道、呼吸、皮肤或循环征象。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Rapid onset of sweating, tremor, hunger, and confusion is characteristic of hypoglycemia."},{"id":17,"concept":"Diabetes","stem":"What is the best immediate treatment for a conscious client with suspected hypoglycemia?","choices":["15 g of fast-acting carbohydrate, then reassess in 15 minutes","A large high-fat meal","Insulin","Nothing by mouth and wait 1 hour"],"answer":0,"why":"The 15-15 approach uses approximately 15 g of fast-acting carbohydrate followed by reassessment after 15 minutes.","zh":"“15-15 法”即给予约 15 克快速吸收碳水化合物，并在 15 分钟后重新评估。","rationales":[{"en":"Fast carbohydrate promptly raises blood glucose.","zh":"快速碳水化合物可迅速升高血糖。"},{"en":"Fat slows glucose absorption and is not ideal for immediate correction.","zh":"脂肪会延缓葡萄糖吸收，不适合立即纠正。"},{"en":"Insulin would worsen hypoglycemia.","zh":"胰岛素会加重低血糖。"},{"en":"Waiting risks progression to unconsciousness or seizure.","zh":"等待可能导致意识丧失或癫痫。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"The 15-15 approach uses approximately 15 g of fast-acting carbohydrate followed by reassessment after 15 minutes."},{"id":18,"concept":"Diabetes","stem":"A client with diabetes is unconscious and suspected of severe hypoglycemia. What is appropriate?","choices":["Give juice by mouth","Call EMS and administer glucagon if trained and available","Place candy under the tongue","Give the client their usual insulin"],"answer":1,"why":"Nothing is given by mouth to an unconscious client. EMS is activated and glucagon may be administered if available and within training.","zh":"昏迷患者不得经口给药。应启动急救服务，并在有药且受过训练时给予胰高血糖素。","rationales":[{"en":"Oral fluids create aspiration risk.","zh":"口服液体会增加误吸风险。"},{"en":"EMS and glucagon are appropriate for severe hypoglycemia.","zh":"急救服务和胰高血糖素适用于重度低血糖。"},{"en":"Candy in the mouth can obstruct the airway.","zh":"将糖果放入口中可能阻塞气道。"},{"en":"Insulin would further lower blood glucose.","zh":"胰岛素会进一步降低血糖。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Nothing is given by mouth to an unconscious client. EMS is activated and glucagon may be administered if available and within training."},{"id":19,"concept":"Diabetes","stem":"Which scheduling advice is best for a client using insulin?","choices":["Skip breakfast before the appointment","Eat normally, take usual medication unless medically directed otherwise, and bring a glucose source","Double insulin before care","Book only after prolonged exercise"],"answer":1,"why":"Normal meals and medication timing reduce hypoglycemia risk, and a rapid glucose source should be available.","zh":"正常进餐和按时用药可降低低血糖风险，并应携带快速补糖来源。","rationales":[{"en":"Skipping meals increases hypoglycemia risk.","zh":"不进餐会增加低血糖风险。"},{"en":"Maintaining routine and carrying glucose is safest.","zh":"保持常规并携带葡萄糖最安全。"},{"en":"Doubling insulin may cause severe hypoglycemia.","zh":"加倍胰岛素可能导致重度低血糖。"},{"en":"Prolonged exercise can lower glucose and complicate timing.","zh":"长时间运动会降低血糖并使预约安排更复杂。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Normal meals and medication timing reduce hypoglycemia risk, and a rapid glucose source should be available."},{"id":20,"concept":"Asthma","stem":"A client with asthma begins wheezing during treatment. What is the first-line medication?","choices":["Short-acting bronchodilator such as salbutamol","Nitroglycerin","Epinephrine auto-injector for every mild episode","Oral glucose"],"answer":0,"why":"A short-acting beta2 agonist is the first-line rescue medication for an acute asthma episode.","zh":"短效 β2 激动剂是急性哮喘发作的一线救援药物。","rationales":[{"en":"A rescue inhaler rapidly bronchodilates.","zh":"救援吸入器可迅速扩张支气管。"},{"en":"Nitroglycerin treats angina, not bronchospasm.","zh":"硝酸甘油治疗心绞痛，而非支气管痉挛。"},{"en":"Epinephrine is reserved for severe asthma unresponsive to inhaler or anaphylaxis, depending on protocol.","zh":"肾上腺素通常用于吸入器无效的严重哮喘或过敏性休克，依方案而定。"},{"en":"Glucose does not reverse bronchospasm.","zh":"葡萄糖不能逆转支气管痉挛。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"A short-acting beta2 agonist is the first-line rescue medication for an acute asthma episode."},{"id":21,"concept":"Asthma","stem":"Which finding suggests an asthma attack is becoming life-threatening?","choices":["Mild wheeze with full sentences","Silent chest, cyanosis, and inability to speak","Occasional cough after water","Stable oxygen saturation and rapid improvement"],"answer":1,"why":"A silent chest with cyanosis and inability to speak indicates minimal airflow and impending respiratory failure.","zh":"“静默胸”、发绀及无法说话提示气流极少和即将发生呼吸衰竭。","rationales":[{"en":"Full sentences suggest less severe respiratory compromise.","zh":"能完整说话通常提示呼吸受损较轻。"},{"en":"These are severe, life-threatening signs.","zh":"这些是严重、危及生命的征象。"},{"en":"An isolated mild cough is not a marker of respiratory failure.","zh":"单纯轻咳不是呼吸衰竭标志。"},{"en":"Rapid improvement and stable oxygenation argue against life-threatening deterioration.","zh":"迅速改善且氧合稳定不支持危及生命的恶化。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"A silent chest with cyanosis and inability to speak indicates minimal airflow and impending respiratory failure."},{"id":22,"concept":"COPD","stem":"Which position is generally best for a client with COPD during dental care?","choices":["Fully supine","Semi-supine or upright","Trendelenburg","Head lower than feet"],"answer":1,"why":"Semi-supine or upright positioning supports diaphragmatic movement and breathing.","zh":"半仰卧或直立体位有助于膈肌运动和呼吸。","rationales":[{"en":"Supine positioning can worsen dyspnea.","zh":"仰卧位可能加重呼吸困难。"},{"en":"An upright posture supports ventilation.","zh":"直立姿势有助于通气。"},{"en":"Trendelenburg can impair breathing.","zh":"特伦德伦堡体位可影响呼吸。"},{"en":"Head-down positioning increases respiratory difficulty.","zh":"头低位会增加呼吸困难。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Semi-supine or upright positioning supports diaphragmatic movement and breathing."},{"id":23,"concept":"COPD","stem":"Why should high-flow oxygen be used cautiously in some clients with severe COPD?","choices":["Oxygen always causes anaphylaxis","Excessive oxygen may reduce hypoxic respiratory drive in susceptible clients","Oxygen causes immediate hypertension","Oxygen destroys bronchodilators"],"answer":1,"why":"Some clients with severe chronic CO2 retention rely partly on hypoxic drive, so oxygen is titrated while monitoring.","zh":"部分严重慢性二氧化碳潴留患者部分依赖低氧驱动，因此应监测并滴定给氧。","rationales":[{"en":"Oxygen does not routinely cause anaphylaxis.","zh":"氧气通常不会引起过敏性休克。"},{"en":"Careful titration is appropriate in susceptible severe COPD.","zh":"对易感的重度 COPD 患者应谨慎滴定。"},{"en":"Immediate hypertension is not the key concern.","zh":"即时高血压不是主要问题。"},{"en":"Oxygen does not chemically destroy inhaled bronchodilators.","zh":"氧气不会化学破坏吸入性支气管扩张剂。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Some clients with severe chronic CO2 retention rely partly on hypoxic drive, so oxygen is titrated while monitoring."},{"id":24,"concept":"Blood Disorders","stem":"A client with hemophilia requires invasive periodontal therapy. What is the best plan?","choices":["Proceed without consultation","Coordinate with the hematology team before invasive care","Stop all factor replacement","Give aspirin before treatment"],"answer":1,"why":"Hemophilia may require factor replacement and a coordinated hemostatic plan before invasive treatment.","zh":"血友病患者在侵入性治疗前可能需要凝血因子替代及协调的止血计划。","rationales":[{"en":"Unplanned invasive care may cause uncontrolled bleeding.","zh":"未经计划的侵入性治疗可能导致无法控制的出血。"},{"en":"Hematology coordination is essential.","zh":"与血液科协调至关重要。"},{"en":"Stopping replacement therapy increases bleeding risk.","zh":"停止替代治疗会增加出血风险。"},{"en":"Aspirin impairs platelet function and may worsen bleeding.","zh":"阿司匹林抑制血小板功能，可能加重出血。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Hemophilia may require factor replacement and a coordinated hemostatic plan before invasive treatment."},{"id":25,"concept":"Blood Disorders","stem":"Which oral finding is commonly associated with thrombocytopenia?","choices":["Petechiae and spontaneous gingival bleeding","Mandibular tori","Geographic tongue only","Enamel hypoplasia"],"answer":0,"why":"Low platelet counts commonly cause petechiae, ecchymoses, and spontaneous mucosal or gingival bleeding.","zh":"血小板减少常引起瘀点、瘀斑及自发性黏膜或牙龈出血。","rationales":[{"en":"These are classic platelet-related bleeding signs.","zh":"这些是典型的血小板相关出血征象。"},{"en":"Tori are benign bony exostoses, not a platelet sign.","zh":"骨隆突是良性骨外生，不是血小板异常征象。"},{"en":"Geographic tongue is unrelated to thrombocytopenic bleeding.","zh":"地图舌与血小板减少性出血无关。"},{"en":"Enamel hypoplasia reflects developmental disturbance, not acute platelet deficiency.","zh":"釉质发育不全反映发育异常，而非急性血小板缺乏。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Low platelet counts commonly cause petechiae, ecchymoses, and spontaneous mucosal or gingival bleeding."},{"id":26,"concept":"Anemia","stem":"A client with significant anemia reports fatigue and shortness of breath. Which modification is best?","choices":["Long appointments with rapid position changes","Short appointments with stress reduction and careful monitoring","Use aspirin for fatigue","Ignore symptoms if the gingiva looks normal"],"answer":1,"why":"Anemia reduces oxygen-carrying capacity, so short low-stress appointments and monitoring are appropriate.","zh":"贫血降低携氧能力，因此应采用短时、低压力预约并仔细监测。","rationales":[{"en":"Long visits and abrupt changes can worsen fatigue and dizziness.","zh":"长时间治疗和突然变换体位会加重疲劳和头晕。"},{"en":"Short low-stress care respects reduced oxygen reserve.","zh":"短时低压力治疗符合氧储备下降的情况。"},{"en":"Aspirin does not treat anemia and can increase bleeding.","zh":"阿司匹林不能治疗贫血，还可能增加出血。"},{"en":"Systemic symptoms require attention regardless of gingival appearance.","zh":"无论牙龈外观如何，全身症状都需重视。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Anemia reduces oxygen-carrying capacity, so short low-stress appointments and monitoring are appropriate."},{"id":27,"concept":"Kidney Disease","stem":"A client receives hemodialysis on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday. When is elective dental hygiene care generally preferred?","choices":["During dialysis","The day after dialysis","Immediately before dialysis after heparin administration","Only on the same evening as dialysis"],"answer":1,"why":"The day after dialysis is often preferred because the client is metabolically optimized and the effect of dialysis heparin has diminished.","zh":"通常选择透析后的第二天，此时患者代谢状态较佳且透析用肝素作用已减弱。","rationales":[{"en":"Treatment during dialysis is impractical and medically inappropriate.","zh":"透析期间进行治疗不实际且医学上不合适。"},{"en":"The day after dialysis is commonly safest.","zh":"透析后的第二天通常最安全。"},{"en":"Heparin exposure can increase bleeding risk.","zh":"肝素暴露会增加出血风险。"},{"en":"Same-evening care may coincide with fatigue and residual anticoagulation.","zh":"同日晚间治疗可能遇到疲劳和残余抗凝作用。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"The day after dialysis is often preferred because the client is metabolically optimized and the effect of dialysis heparin has diminished."},{"id":28,"concept":"Kidney Disease","stem":"Which medication concern is especially relevant in advanced kidney disease?","choices":["All drugs are eliminated only by the lungs","Renally cleared drugs may accumulate and require dose adjustment","Local anesthetic never works","Antibiotics are always contraindicated"],"answer":1,"why":"Reduced renal clearance can prolong drug half-life and cause accumulation, so prescriber consultation or dose adjustment may be needed.","zh":"肾清除率下降可延长药物半衰期并导致蓄积，因此可能需要会诊或调整剂量。","rationales":[{"en":"Many drugs are metabolized or excreted through liver and kidneys, not only lungs.","zh":"许多药物经肝脏代谢或肾脏排泄，并非仅由肺排出。"},{"en":"Renal impairment can cause drug accumulation.","zh":"肾功能不全可导致药物蓄积。"},{"en":"Local anesthetic efficacy is not universally lost in kidney disease.","zh":"肾病并不会普遍导致局部麻醉无效。"},{"en":"Some antibiotics can be used with appropriate selection and dosing.","zh":"某些抗生素可在正确选择和调整剂量后使用。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Reduced renal clearance can prolong drug half-life and cause accumulation, so prescriber consultation or dose adjustment may be needed."},{"id":29,"concept":"Liver Disease","stem":"Why is medication review important in severe liver disease?","choices":["The liver has no role in drug handling","Impaired hepatic metabolism can increase drug levels and toxicity","All drugs become ineffective","Only topical agents are affected"],"answer":1,"why":"The liver metabolizes many medications; severe impairment can increase circulating drug levels and adverse effects.","zh":"肝脏代谢许多药物；严重肝功能受损可增加血药浓度和不良反应。","rationales":[{"en":"The liver is central to metabolism of many drugs.","zh":"肝脏是许多药物代谢的核心器官。"},{"en":"Reduced hepatic metabolism increases toxicity risk.","zh":"肝代谢下降会增加毒性风险。"},{"en":"Drugs do not all become ineffective; some become more potent or prolonged.","zh":"药物并非都失效，有些作用会增强或延长。"},{"en":"Systemic drugs are especially affected, not only topical agents.","zh":"受影响的尤其是全身用药，而不只是局部药物。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"The liver metabolizes many medications; severe impairment can increase circulating drug levels and adverse effects."},{"id":30,"concept":"Hepatitis","stem":"Which infection-control statement is correct for a client with hepatitis B?","choices":["Use special precautions only if the client reports active symptoms","Apply standard precautions to every client","Refuse all care permanently","Double-glove only for hepatitis B and no one else"],"answer":1,"why":"Standard precautions are used consistently for all clients because infection status may be unknown.","zh":"由于感染状态可能未知，应对所有患者一致采用标准预防措施。","rationales":[{"en":"Relying on symptoms misses asymptomatic and undisclosed infection.","zh":"依赖症状会漏掉无症状或未披露的感染。"},{"en":"Standard precautions apply universally.","zh":"标准预防措施适用于所有患者。"},{"en":"Hepatitis B does not justify permanent refusal of care.","zh":"乙型肝炎不构成永久拒绝治疗的理由。"},{"en":"PPE decisions are based on exposure risk, not a single diagnosis alone.","zh":"个人防护装备应依据暴露风险，而非仅针对某一诊断。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Standard precautions are used consistently for all clients because infection status may be unknown."},{"id":31,"concept":"Thyroid Disorders","stem":"A client with uncontrolled hyperthyroidism requires elective care. What is the best action?","choices":["Proceed and use maximum epinephrine","Defer elective care and obtain medical stabilization","Give thyroid hormone","Use long stressful appointments"],"answer":1,"why":"Uncontrolled hyperthyroidism increases risk of thyroid storm and exaggerated catecholamine response, so elective care is deferred.","zh":"未控制的甲状腺功能亢进会增加甲状腺危象和儿茶酚胺过度反应风险，因此应推迟选择性治疗。","rationales":[{"en":"Epinephrine may intensify tachycardia and precipitate crisis.","zh":"肾上腺素可能加重心动过速并诱发危象。"},{"en":"Medical stabilization is required before elective care.","zh":"选择性治疗前需先实现医学稳定。"},{"en":"Thyroid hormone would worsen hyperthyroidism.","zh":"甲状腺激素会加重甲亢。"},{"en":"Stress can provoke dangerous symptoms.","zh":"压力可能诱发危险症状。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Uncontrolled hyperthyroidism increases risk of thyroid storm and exaggerated catecholamine response, so elective care is deferred."},{"id":32,"concept":"Adrenal Disorders","stem":"A client on long-term high-dose corticosteroids may be at risk for which problem during major stress?","choices":["Adrenal insufficiency","Hyperthyroidism","Iron overload","Insulinoma"],"answer":0,"why":"Chronic corticosteroid therapy can suppress the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis, reducing the stress response.","zh":"长期糖皮质激素治疗可抑制下丘脑-垂体-肾上腺轴，降低应激反应。","rationales":[{"en":"Adrenal suppression is the key concern.","zh":"主要问题是肾上腺抑制。"},{"en":"Corticosteroid use does not directly cause hyperthyroidism.","zh":"糖皮质激素使用不会直接导致甲亢。"},{"en":"Iron overload is unrelated to adrenal suppression.","zh":"铁过载与肾上腺抑制无关。"},{"en":"Insulinoma is a pancreatic tumor, not a steroid-withdrawal effect.","zh":"胰岛素瘤是胰腺肿瘤，并非停用激素的影响。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Chronic corticosteroid therapy can suppress the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis, reducing the stress response."},{"id":33,"concept":"Pregnancy","stem":"Which positioning modification is appropriate in late pregnancy?","choices":["Prolonged flat supine position","Slight left lateral tilt or semi-supine position","Trendelenburg for the full appointment","Prone position"],"answer":1,"why":"A slight left tilt reduces compression of the inferior vena cava by the gravid uterus and helps prevent supine hypotensive syndrome.","zh":"轻度左侧倾斜可减少妊娠子宫对下腔静脉的压迫，并预防仰卧位低血压综合征。","rationales":[{"en":"Prolonged supine positioning can reduce venous return.","zh":"长时间仰卧可减少静脉回流。"},{"en":"Left tilt or semi-supine positioning is appropriate.","zh":"左侧倾斜或半仰卧体位合适。"},{"en":"Trendelenburg may worsen discomfort and breathing.","zh":"特伦德伦堡体位可能加重不适和呼吸困难。"},{"en":"Prone positioning is not feasible in late pregnancy.","zh":"妊娠晚期不适合俯卧位。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"A slight left tilt reduces compression of the inferior vena cava by the gravid uterus and helps prevent supine hypotensive syndrome."},{"id":34,"concept":"Pregnancy","stem":"Which trimester is generally preferred for routine elective dental care?","choices":["First trimester only","Second trimester","Only the final month","No dental care during pregnancy"],"answer":1,"why":"The second trimester is often most comfortable and avoids the early period of organogenesis and late-pregnancy positioning challenges.","zh":"第二孕期通常最舒适，也避开早期器官形成期和晚期体位困难。","rationales":[{"en":"Urgent care can be provided in any trimester, but the first is not the preferred elective window.","zh":"任何孕期都可进行急症治疗，但第一孕期不是首选选择性治疗时间。"},{"en":"The second trimester is generally preferred.","zh":"通常首选第二孕期。"},{"en":"The final month often has greater discomfort and supine hypotension risk.","zh":"最后一个月通常不适更明显，仰卧低血压风险更高。"},{"en":"Necessary dental care should not be withheld throughout pregnancy.","zh":"不应在整个孕期拒绝必要的牙科治疗。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"The second trimester is often most comfortable and avoids the early period of organogenesis and late-pregnancy positioning challenges."},{"id":35,"concept":"Tuberculosis","stem":"A client has suspected active infectious tuberculosis. What is the best approach to elective care?","choices":["Provide routine elective care with standard mask only","Defer elective care and refer for medical assessment; provide urgent care in an appropriate airborne-infection setting","Schedule at the busiest time of day","Use only a rubber dam"],"answer":1,"why":"Active infectious TB requires airborne precautions and medical management; routine elective dental care is deferred.","zh":"活动性传染性结核需要空气传播隔离和医学管理，常规选择性牙科治疗应推迟。","rationales":[{"en":"A standard surgical mask alone does not provide adequate airborne protection.","zh":"普通外科口罩不足以提供空气传播防护。"},{"en":"Deferral and proper medical/airborne management are appropriate.","zh":"推迟治疗并进行适当医学和空气隔离管理是正确做法。"},{"en":"A busy clinic increases exposure risk.","zh":"繁忙诊所会增加暴露风险。"},{"en":"A rubber dam does not eliminate airborne transmission risk.","zh":"橡皮障不能消除空气传播风险。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Active infectious TB requires airborne precautions and medical management; routine elective dental care is deferred."},{"id":36,"concept":"HIV/AIDS","stem":"Which statement about dental care for a client with HIV is correct?","choices":["Standard precautions are sufficient for routine care","The client must always be treated last","All invasive care is prohibited","The chart should be visibly labeled for staff warning"],"answer":0,"why":"Standard precautions are designed for all clients. Care is based on current health status, medications, and relevant laboratory information, not stigma.","zh":"标准预防措施适用于所有患者。治疗应依据当前健康状况、用药及相关实验室资料，而非污名化。","rationales":[{"en":"Standard precautions are appropriate.","zh":"标准预防措施是恰当的。"},{"en":"Scheduling last is not required and may be discriminatory.","zh":"不要求最后预约，这可能构成歧视。"},{"en":"HIV does not automatically prohibit invasive care.","zh":"HIV 并不自动禁止侵入性治疗。"},{"en":"Visible warning labels breach confidentiality and are inappropriate.","zh":"显眼警示标签侵犯隐私，并不合适。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Standard precautions are designed for all clients. Care is based on current health status, medications, and relevant laboratory information, not stigma."},{"id":37,"concept":"HIV/AIDS","stem":"Which oral finding is strongly associated with immunosuppression in HIV?","choices":["Oral candidiasis","Mandibular tori","Fordyce granules","Linea alba"],"answer":0,"why":"Oral candidiasis is a common opportunistic infection and may reflect immune suppression.","zh":"口腔念珠菌病是常见机会性感染，可反映免疫抑制。","rationales":[{"en":"Candidiasis is associated with reduced immune function.","zh":"念珠菌病与免疫功能降低相关。"},{"en":"Tori are benign anatomic variations.","zh":"骨隆突是良性解剖变异。"},{"en":"Fordyce granules are ectopic sebaceous glands and are usually normal.","zh":"福代斯颗粒为异位皮脂腺，通常属正常。"},{"en":"Linea alba is a frictional change, not an opportunistic infection.","zh":"白线是摩擦性改变，不是机会性感染。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Oral candidiasis is a common opportunistic infection and may reflect immune suppression."},{"id":38,"concept":"Developmental Disabilities","stem":"What is the best behavioral approach for a client with an intellectual disability who is anxious about care?","choices":["Use tell-show-do, short visits, and positive reinforcement","Use surprise procedures to reduce anticipation","Speak rapidly and use abstract explanations","Exclude the caregiver even when support is helpful and consent allows"],"answer":0,"why":"Tell-show-do, predictable routines, short visits, and positive reinforcement improve understanding and trust.","zh":"“讲解-展示-操作”、可预测流程、短时预约和正向强化可提升理解与信任。","rationales":[{"en":"This structured approach supports cooperation.","zh":"这种结构化方法有助于配合。"},{"en":"Surprise procedures can increase fear and reduce trust.","zh":"突然操作会增加恐惧并降低信任。"},{"en":"Rapid abstract language is harder to process.","zh":"快速抽象语言更难理解。"},{"en":"A supportive caregiver may be helpful when appropriate and permitted.","zh":"在合适且获准时，支持性照护者可能很有帮助。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Tell-show-do, predictable routines, short visits, and positive reinforcement improve understanding and trust."},{"id":39,"concept":"Autism","stem":"Which environmental modification may help a client with autism who has sensory sensitivity?","choices":["Increase lighting, noise, and conversation","Reduce sensory stimulation and keep the visit predictable","Change clinicians repeatedly","Use strong-flavoured products without warning"],"answer":1,"why":"Reducing noise, light, strong tastes, and unexpected changes can lower sensory overload and anxiety.","zh":"减少噪音、强光、强烈味道和意外变化可降低感官过载与焦虑。","rationales":[{"en":"More stimulation may worsen sensory overload.","zh":"更多刺激可能加重感官过载。"},{"en":"A calm predictable environment is helpful.","zh":"平静且可预测的环境有帮助。"},{"en":"Consistency of staff often improves comfort.","zh":"人员一致性通常可提高舒适度。"},{"en":"Unexpected strong flavours may trigger distress.","zh":"意外的强烈味道可能引发不适。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Reducing noise, light, strong tastes, and unexpected changes can lower sensory overload and anxiety."},{"id":40,"concept":"Medical Consultation","stem":"Which situation most clearly requires medical consultation before elective dental hygiene care?","choices":["Stable, well-controlled asthma with rescue inhaler available","Unexplained recent syncope and new chest pain","A healed paper cut","Mild seasonal allergies"],"answer":1,"why":"New unexplained syncope combined with chest pain may indicate serious cardiovascular disease and requires medical evaluation before elective care.","zh":"近期不明原因晕厥并伴新发胸痛可能提示严重心血管疾病，选择性治疗前需医学评估。","rationales":[{"en":"Stable controlled asthma can usually be managed with routine modifications.","zh":"稳定且控制良好的哮喘通常可通过常规调整进行治疗。"},{"en":"This combination is a red flag requiring consultation.","zh":"这一组合是需要会诊的危险信号。"},{"en":"A healed minor cut does not require consultation.","zh":"已愈合的小伤口无需会诊。"},{"en":"Mild seasonal allergies alone do not usually require medical clearance.","zh":"单纯轻度季节性过敏通常不需要医学许可。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"New unexplained syncope combined with chest pain may indicate serious cardiovascular disease and requires medical evaluation before elective care."},{"id":41,"concept":"Dialysis and Kidney Disease","stem":"A client receives hemodialysis on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday. When is routine dental hygiene care generally best scheduled?","choices":["During dialysis","Later the same day after dialysis","On a non-dialysis day, commonly the day after dialysis","Only immediately before dialysis"],"answer":2,"why":"A non-dialysis day, often the day after treatment, avoids intravascular heparin effects and allows the client to recover from dialysis-related fatigue.","zh":"常规牙科卫生治疗通常安排在非透析日，常见选择是透析后的第二天，以避开肝素抗凝作用并让患者从透析疲劳中恢复。","rationales":[{"en":"Treatment during dialysis is not a routine dental setting and the client may be medically unstable.","zh":"透析过程中并非常规牙科治疗环境，患者也可能医学状况不稳定。"},{"en":"The same day may involve residual anticoagulation and significant fatigue.","zh":"透析当天可能仍有抗凝作用并伴明显疲劳。"},{"en":"A non-dialysis day reduces bleeding and fatigue concerns.","zh":"非透析日可减少出血和疲劳方面的担忧。"},{"en":"Immediately before dialysis may be inconvenient and does not provide the usual post-dialysis benefit.","zh":"透析前立即治疗通常不便，也没有透析后体液状态改善的优势。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Schedule routine care on a non-dialysis day, commonly the day after hemodialysis."},{"id":42,"concept":"Dialysis and Kidney Disease","stem":"Which arm should generally be avoided for blood-pressure measurement in a client with an arteriovenous dialysis fistula?","choices":["The arm with the fistula","The arm without the fistula","Both arms permanently","Neither arm if the client feels well"],"answer":0,"why":"Pressure and trauma to the fistula arm can compromise vascular access, so blood pressure and venipuncture are avoided on that side.","zh":"瘘管侧手臂应避免测量血压或静脉穿刺，因为压力和创伤可能损害透析血管通路。","rationales":[{"en":"Protecting the fistula arm preserves essential vascular access.","zh":"保护瘘管侧手臂可维持重要的血管通路。"},{"en":"The opposite arm is generally used when appropriate.","zh":"在合适情况下通常使用对侧手臂。"},{"en":"Blood pressure is not permanently prohibited in both arms.","zh":"并非永久禁止在双臂测量血压。"},{"en":"Feeling well does not remove the need to protect the fistula.","zh":"即使感觉良好，也必须保护瘘管。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Do not compress or traumatize an arteriovenous fistula arm."},{"id":43,"concept":"Liver Disease","stem":"Which concern is most important when planning invasive care for a client with advanced liver disease?","choices":["Reduced clotting-factor production and altered drug metabolism","Excess enamel formation","Increased salivary buffering only","Improved tolerance of hepatically metabolized drugs"],"answer":0,"why":"Advanced liver disease may impair coagulation and drug metabolism, increasing bleeding and medication-toxicity risks.","zh":"晚期肝病可能损害凝血因子生成及药物代谢，从而增加出血和药物毒性风险。","rationales":[{"en":"Both coagulation and hepatic drug clearance may be impaired.","zh":"凝血功能和肝脏药物清除均可能受损。"},{"en":"Liver disease does not cause excess enamel formation.","zh":"肝病不会导致牙釉质过度形成。"},{"en":"Salivary buffering is not the primary invasive-care concern.","zh":"唾液缓冲并不是侵入性治疗的主要风险。"},{"en":"Tolerance may be reduced, not improved, when metabolism is impaired.","zh":"代谢受损时药物耐受性可能下降，而非提高。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Advanced liver disease raises both bleeding and medication-metabolism concerns."},{"id":44,"concept":"Bleeding Disorders","stem":"A client with severe hemophilia requires invasive periodontal instrumentation. What is the best plan?","choices":["Proceed without consultation because local pressure is always sufficient","Coordinate with the hematology team before treatment","Ask the client to stop factor replacement","Give aspirin before care"],"answer":1,"why":"Severe hemophilia may require factor replacement or another hemostatic plan coordinated with the hematology team before invasive procedures.","zh":"重度血友病患者进行侵入性牙周操作前，可能需要凝血因子替代或其他止血方案，应与血液科团队协调。","rationales":[{"en":"Local pressure alone may be inadequate in severe factor deficiency.","zh":"严重凝血因子缺乏时，仅局部加压可能不足。"},{"en":"Specialist coordination establishes a safe hemostatic plan.","zh":"与专科团队协调可制定安全的止血计划。"},{"en":"Stopping prescribed factor therapy increases bleeding risk.","zh":"停用处方凝血因子治疗会增加出血风险。"},{"en":"Aspirin impairs platelet function and can worsen bleeding.","zh":"阿司匹林抑制血小板功能，可能加重出血。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Severe bleeding disorders require a coordinated hemostatic plan before invasive care."},{"id":45,"concept":"Cancer Therapy","stem":"A client receiving chemotherapy has a fever and a very low neutrophil count. What is the best approach to elective dental hygiene care?","choices":["Proceed with ultrasonic debridement","Defer elective care and contact the oncology team","Provide care only if the client takes aspirin","Ignore the laboratory findings if oral tissues look normal"],"answer":1,"why":"Fever with severe neutropenia signals high infection risk. Elective care should be deferred and the oncology team consulted.","zh":"发热并伴严重中性粒细胞减少提示感染风险很高，应推迟选择性治疗并联系肿瘤科团队。","rationales":[{"en":"Instrumentation can introduce infection when immune defenses are severely reduced.","zh":"免疫防御严重下降时，器械操作可能引入感染。"},{"en":"Deferral and oncology consultation address the systemic risk.","zh":"推迟治疗并与肿瘤科会诊可处理全身风险。"},{"en":"Aspirin does not correct neutropenia and may increase bleeding.","zh":"阿司匹林不能纠正中性粒细胞减少，还可能增加出血。"},{"en":"Normal-looking tissues do not negate the systemic laboratory risk.","zh":"口腔组织外观正常并不能排除全身实验室风险。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Fever plus severe neutropenia is a red flag for deferring elective care."},{"id":46,"concept":"Cancer Therapy","stem":"What is the most appropriate oral-care emphasis for a client undergoing head-and-neck radiation who develops xerostomia?","choices":["Frequent sugar-containing lozenges","Daily high-fluoride prevention and meticulous plaque control","Discontinue all brushing","Use alcohol-based rinses frequently"],"answer":1,"why":"Radiation-related xerostomia greatly increases caries risk, making intensive fluoride exposure, plaque control, and saliva-support strategies important.","zh":"头颈部放疗引起的口干会显著增加龋病风险，因此应加强高氟防龋、菌斑控制及唾液支持措施。","rationales":[{"en":"Sugar-containing products increase caries risk in a dry mouth.","zh":"口干时含糖产品会增加龋病风险。"},{"en":"High-fluoride prevention and plaque control directly address radiation caries risk.","zh":"高氟防龋和菌斑控制可直接降低放射性龋风险。"},{"en":"Stopping brushing permits rapid plaque accumulation.","zh":"停止刷牙会导致菌斑快速堆积。"},{"en":"Alcohol-containing rinses may worsen dryness and irritation.","zh":"含酒精漱口水可能加重干燥和刺激。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Head-and-neck radiation xerostomia requires aggressive caries prevention."},{"id":47,"concept":"Organ Transplant","stem":"A client taking immunosuppressive medication after an organ transplant presents for care. Which action is most appropriate?","choices":["Assume infection risk is normal","Review current immune status, medications, and coordinate care when indicated","Stop the immunosuppressant before instrumentation","Use visible chart warnings about the transplant"],"answer":1,"why":"Transplant recipients may have increased infection risk, altered healing, and medication-related oral effects, so current status and medical guidance should be reviewed.","zh":"器官移植患者可能有感染风险增加、愈合改变及药物相关口腔反应，因此应审查其当前状况、用药，并在需要时进行医学协调。","rationales":[{"en":"Immunosuppression can substantially alter infection risk.","zh":"免疫抑制可能显著改变感染风险。"},{"en":"Individualized review supports safe treatment planning.","zh":"个体化评估有助于安全制定治疗计划。"},{"en":"The dental hygienist should not independently stop transplant medication.","zh":"牙科卫生师不应自行停用移植药物。"},{"en":"Visible warnings can breach confidentiality and promote stigma.","zh":"显眼警示可能侵犯隐私并造成污名。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Transplant care is individualized according to immune status, medications, and medical guidance."},{"id":48,"concept":"Organ Transplant","stem":"Which oral change is commonly associated with some immunosuppressive regimens used after transplantation?","choices":["Gingival enlargement","Complete absence of plaque","Permanent enamel whitening","Immediate tooth ankylosis"],"answer":0,"why":"Some immunosuppressive drugs, particularly calcineurin inhibitors, can contribute to gingival enlargement, especially when plaque control is poor.","zh":"某些移植后免疫抑制药，尤其钙调神经磷酸酶抑制剂，可导致牙龈增生，菌斑控制不佳时更明显。","rationales":[{"en":"Gingival enlargement is a recognized medication-related oral effect.","zh":"牙龈增生是已知的药物相关口腔反应。"},{"en":"Immunosuppressants do not eliminate plaque.","zh":"免疫抑制药不会消除菌斑。"},{"en":"They do not permanently whiten enamel.","zh":"这些药物不会使牙釉质永久变白。"},{"en":"Tooth ankylosis is not an expected immediate drug effect.","zh":"牙齿强直并非预期的即时药物反应。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Some transplant medications can cause gingival enlargement."},{"id":49,"concept":"Parkinson Disease","stem":"Which modification is most helpful for a client with Parkinson disease who has tremor and difficulty maintaining oral hygiene?","choices":["Recommend a large-handled or powered toothbrush and caregiver support as needed","Use only written instructions in small print","Schedule long appointments late in the day","Discourage all adaptive devices"],"answer":0,"why":"Adaptive handles, powered brushes, simplified routines, and caregiver assistance can compensate for tremor and reduced dexterity.","zh":"加粗手柄、电动牙刷、简化流程及必要时照护者协助，可弥补震颤和精细动作能力下降。","rationales":[{"en":"Adaptive devices directly address motor limitations.","zh":"辅助装置可直接应对运动功能受限。"},{"en":"Small-print written instructions may be difficult to use and do not address dexterity.","zh":"小字书面说明可能难以使用，也不能解决手部灵活性问题。"},{"en":"Fatigue and medication wearing-off may make late long visits harder.","zh":"疲劳及药效减弱可能使下午长时预约更加困难。"},{"en":"Avoiding adaptive devices removes useful support.","zh":"拒绝辅助装置会失去有益支持。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Use adaptive oral-hygiene aids to compensate for tremor and reduced dexterity."},{"id":50,"concept":"Dementia","stem":"A client with moderate dementia becomes confused during a long appointment. What is the best modification?","choices":["Use a short, familiar, predictable visit and simple one-step instructions","Add multiple unfamiliar staff members","Provide complex explanations without repetition","Continue despite escalating distress"],"answer":0,"why":"Short predictable appointments, familiar routines, and simple instructions reduce cognitive load and distress.","zh":"短时、熟悉且可预测的预约，以及简单的一步式指令，可降低认知负担和不安。","rationales":[{"en":"This approach supports orientation and cooperation.","zh":"这种方法有助于定向和配合。"},{"en":"Unfamiliar people can increase confusion.","zh":"陌生人员可能增加混乱。"},{"en":"Complex instructions exceed the client’s processing capacity.","zh":"复杂说明可能超过患者的处理能力。"},{"en":"Continuing through escalating distress is unsafe and undermines consent.","zh":"在不安加剧时继续治疗不安全，也不符合有效同意。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"For dementia, simplify, shorten, and keep the visit predictable."},{"id":51,"concept":"Stroke Adaptations","stem":"A client has right-sided weakness after a stroke. Which home-care recommendation is most appropriate?","choices":["Use an adapted toothbrush and train the stronger hand","Stop all interdental cleaning permanently","Use the weak hand only to force rehabilitation","Avoid caregiver involvement even with permission"],"answer":0,"why":"Adaptive devices and use of the stronger side can support safe independent oral hygiene; caregiver help may be added with consent.","zh":"辅助牙刷及使用较强一侧可支持安全独立的口腔清洁；在获得同意时也可加入照护者协助。","rationales":[{"en":"This approach works with the client’s remaining motor function.","zh":"这种方法利用患者保留的运动功能。"},{"en":"Interdental care should be adapted, not automatically abandoned.","zh":"牙间清洁应进行调整，而不是自动放弃。"},{"en":"Forcing the weak hand may be ineffective or unsafe without rehabilitation guidance.","zh":"未经康复指导强迫使用无力侧可能无效或不安全。"},{"en":"Permitted caregiver support can improve daily care.","zh":"获准的照护者支持可改善日常护理。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Match home-care aids to the client’s remaining strength and dexterity."},{"id":52,"concept":"Mobility and Arthritis","stem":"A client with severe rheumatoid arthritis cannot grip a conventional toothbrush. Which recommendation is best?","choices":["Enlarge the handle or use a powered toothbrush","Use a smaller, thinner handle","Stop brushing painful days","Recommend only mouthrinse"],"answer":0,"why":"A built-up handle or powered toothbrush reduces the grip strength and fine motor control needed for effective brushing.","zh":"加粗手柄或电动牙刷可降低有效刷牙所需的握力和精细动作要求。","rationales":[{"en":"This modification improves access despite limited grip.","zh":"这种调整可在握力受限时改善清洁能力。"},{"en":"A thinner handle is usually harder to grasp.","zh":"更细的手柄通常更难握持。"},{"en":"Skipping brushing permits plaque accumulation.","zh":"停止刷牙会导致菌斑堆积。"},{"en":"Mouthrinse alone does not replace mechanical plaque removal.","zh":"仅使用漱口水不能替代机械清除菌斑。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Build up the handle or use powered devices when grip is limited."},{"id":53,"concept":"Autism","stem":"A client with autism is distressed by unexpected sounds and flavours. What should the dental hygienist do before treatment?","choices":["Preview the sequence and sensory stimuli, then offer controlled choices","Introduce strong flavours without warning","Change the plan repeatedly","Use restraint as the first strategy"],"answer":0,"why":"Advance preparation, predictable sequencing, and controlled choices can reduce sensory overload and improve cooperation.","zh":"提前说明流程和感官刺激，并提供有限可控的选择，可减少感官过载并提高配合。","rationales":[{"en":"Preparation and predictability support sensory regulation.","zh":"准备和可预测性有助于感官调节。"},{"en":"Unexpected strong flavours can trigger distress.","zh":"意外的强烈味道可能引发不安。"},{"en":"Repeated changes reduce predictability.","zh":"反复改变计划会降低可预测性。"},{"en":"Restraint is not a routine first-line behavioural approach.","zh":"约束并非常规的一线行为管理方法。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Preview sensory experiences and preserve predictability for autistic clients."},{"id":54,"concept":"Developmental Disabilities","stem":"An adult client with a developmental disability can understand the proposed care and communicate a choice. Who should provide consent?","choices":["The client","A caregiver automatically","Any staff member","The clinician without discussion"],"answer":0,"why":"Capacity is decision-specific. A capable adult gives their own informed consent even when a caregiver is involved in support.","zh":"同意能力取决于具体决定。即使有照护者参与支持，具备能力的成年患者仍应自行作出知情同意。","rationales":[{"en":"A capable adult retains autonomy and provides consent.","zh":"有能力的成年人保有自主权并自行同意。"},{"en":"A caregiver does not automatically replace a capable client’s decision.","zh":"照护者不会自动取代有能力患者的决定。"},{"en":"Unrelated staff cannot provide consent without legal authority.","zh":"无合法授权的工作人员不能代为同意。"},{"en":"Treatment without discussion violates informed-consent requirements.","zh":"未经讨论直接治疗违反知情同意要求。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Do not confuse disability with incapacity; assess the specific decision."},{"id":55,"concept":"Pregnancy","stem":"A pregnant client develops dizziness, pallor, and nausea while lying supine. What is the best immediate action?","choices":["Turn the client toward the left side","Keep the client flat and continue","Place the client prone","Ask the client to stand quickly"],"answer":0,"why":"Left lateral positioning relieves uterine compression of the inferior vena cava and improves venous return in supine hypotensive syndrome.","zh":"左侧卧位可减轻妊娠子宫对下腔静脉的压迫，并改善仰卧位低血压综合征中的静脉回流。","rationales":[{"en":"Left positioning addresses the likely vena-caval compression.","zh":"左侧体位可处理可能的下腔静脉受压。"},{"en":"Remaining supine can worsen hypotension.","zh":"继续仰卧可能加重低血压。"},{"en":"Prone positioning is not appropriate in pregnancy.","zh":"妊娠期不适合俯卧位。"},{"en":"Standing suddenly increases fall and syncope risk.","zh":"突然站立会增加跌倒和晕厥风险。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"For supine hypotensive symptoms in pregnancy, turn the client to the left."},{"id":56,"concept":"Breastfeeding","stem":"A breastfeeding client needs routine dental hygiene care. Which statement is most appropriate?","choices":["Routine preventive care is generally compatible with breastfeeding","All dental radiographs are permanently contraindicated","The client must stop breastfeeding before any local anesthetic","Oral hygiene instruction should be postponed until weaning"],"answer":0,"why":"Routine preventive dental care is generally compatible with breastfeeding; medication or imaging questions are assessed individually rather than by blanket prohibition.","zh":"常规预防性牙科护理通常与哺乳相容；药物或影像问题应个别评估，而非一概禁止。","rationales":[{"en":"Breastfeeding is not a reason to defer routine preventive care.","zh":"哺乳并不是推迟常规预防护理的理由。"},{"en":"Necessary dental imaging is not permanently prohibited solely because of breastfeeding.","zh":"仅因哺乳并不永久禁止必要的牙科影像检查。"},{"en":"Many local anesthetic decisions can be made safely without routine cessation of breastfeeding.","zh":"许多局部麻醉可在无需常规停止哺乳的情况下安全使用。"},{"en":"Oral-health education remains beneficial during breastfeeding.","zh":"哺乳期间口腔健康教育仍然有益。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Breastfeeding rarely requires blanket postponement of routine dental care."},{"id":57,"concept":"Cardiac Devices","stem":"A client with a modern implanted cardiac device requires ultrasonic instrumentation. What is the best approach?","choices":["Confirm device compatibility and follow current manufacturer or medical guidance","Assume every ultrasonic unit is prohibited forever","Place the ultrasonic cable directly over the device","Disable the cardiac device before care"],"answer":0,"why":"Device type and equipment compatibility vary; current guidance should be confirmed rather than applying a universal ban or altering the device.","zh":"心脏装置和设备兼容性各不相同，应确认当前制造商或医疗指导，而不是一概禁止或自行更改装置。","rationales":[{"en":"Compatibility review is individualized and evidence-based.","zh":"兼容性审查应个体化并基于证据。"},{"en":"A permanent universal ban is unnecessarily broad.","zh":"永久全面禁止过于宽泛。"},{"en":"Positioning equipment directly over the device may increase interference risk.","zh":"将设备直接置于植入装置上方可能增加干扰风险。"},{"en":"The dental hygienist must not disable an implanted cardiac device.","zh":"牙科卫生师不得关闭植入式心脏装置。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Confirm compatibility instead of assuming all ultrasonics are prohibited."},{"id":58,"concept":"Infective Endocarditis","stem":"A client reports a heart murmur but is unsure whether antibiotic prophylaxis is required. What is the best action before an invasive procedure?","choices":["Prescribe antibiotics automatically","Clarify the cardiac diagnosis and current prophylaxis recommendation with the appropriate prescriber","Proceed and decide after treatment","Tell the client to double a previous antibiotic dose"],"answer":1,"why":"A murmur alone does not establish prophylaxis need. The specific cardiac condition and current recommendation must be confirmed before invasive care.","zh":"单纯心脏杂音并不能确定是否需要预防性抗生素。侵入性治疗前应确认具体心脏诊断及当前预防建议。","rationales":[{"en":"Automatic prophylaxis exposes the client to unnecessary medication risk.","zh":"自动给予预防性抗生素会带来不必要的用药风险。"},{"en":"Clarification supports correct, current, condition-specific care.","zh":"确认诊断可确保治疗符合当前且针对具体病情的建议。"},{"en":"The decision must be made before, not after, the invasive procedure.","zh":"应在侵入性治疗前而不是之后作出决定。"},{"en":"The client should not independently alter an old antibiotic regimen.","zh":"患者不应自行更改旧的抗生素方案。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"A heart murmur is not enough information; verify the exact cardiac condition."},{"id":59,"concept":"ASA Classification","stem":"A client has poorly controlled diabetes with significant systemic complications but is not in immediate life-threatening crisis. Which ASA classification is most appropriate?","choices":["ASA I","ASA II","ASA III","ASA IV"],"answer":2,"why":"Poorly controlled disease with significant systemic impact generally represents severe systemic disease and fits ASA III when it is not a constant threat to life.","zh":"控制不良且造成显著全身影响的糖尿病通常属于严重全身性疾病；若并非持续威胁生命，通常归为 ASA III。","rationales":[{"en":"ASA I is limited to healthy clients.","zh":"ASA I 仅适用于健康患者。"},{"en":"ASA II is too low for poorly controlled disease with complications.","zh":"对控制不良并有并发症的疾病而言，ASA II 过低。"},{"en":"ASA III matches severe systemic disease without a constant life threat.","zh":"ASA III 适用于严重但并非持续威胁生命的全身性疾病。"},{"en":"ASA IV requires disease that is a constant threat to life.","zh":"ASA IV 要求疾病持续威胁生命。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Severe systemic disease without a constant life threat is generally ASA III."},{"id":60,"concept":"Integrated Case","stem":"A client with end-stage kidney disease, a dialysis fistula, warfarin therapy, and fatigue presents the morning after dialysis. Which plan is best?","choices":["Use the fistula arm for blood pressure and proceed without review","Review bleeding risk, avoid the fistula arm, assess current condition, and use local hemostatic measures as needed","Tell the client to stop warfarin immediately","Reschedule care for during the next dialysis session"],"answer":1,"why":"Safe care integrates dialysis timing, fistula protection, anticoagulation assessment, current symptoms, and local bleeding control without independently stopping medication.","zh":"安全治疗应综合考虑透析时间、瘘管保护、抗凝评估、当前症状及局部止血，而不能自行停药。","rationales":[{"en":"The fistula arm must be protected and anticoagulation cannot be ignored.","zh":"必须保护瘘管侧手臂，也不能忽视抗凝治疗。"},{"en":"This plan addresses the client’s interacting medical risks comprehensively.","zh":"该计划可全面处理患者相互作用的医学风险。"},{"en":"Independent warfarin cessation can cause thromboembolic harm.","zh":"自行停用华法林可能造成血栓栓塞伤害。"},{"en":"Dialysis is not the appropriate setting for routine dental hygiene care.","zh":"透析过程中并非常规牙科卫生治疗的合适环境。"}],"level":"NDHCE-style","pearl":"Integrated planning must address dialysis, fistula protection, anticoagulation, and current symptoms together."}];
window.FULL_BANK=SN_BANK;
